  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Kess-who-counted
    
    Nightshelf miner and extraction tally-keeper at ☽'scar Ramtatus~, the colony's primary fire-core mining complex. Kess tracked yields across the deep shafts and was the first to report that output from shafts six through twelve was declining while the veins themselves showed no depletion — evidence that something was consuming heat before harvest. The colony's leadership, constrained by Flipper Accord production quotas, classified the anomaly as ordinary vein exhaustion. Kess's numbers were not refuted. They were reclassified.
    
    The chronicle of ☽'Lucatransiius Glow-bringer, a Pactum∴ne enforcer of an earlier generation, describes discovering an identical unexplained cold in shaft eight — and making the identical decision to report it as depletion. That two observers separated by considerable time reached the same finding and met the same institutional response suggests the anomaly was neither new nor unknown. It was managed.
    
    ### The Zen∴ctum Collapse and After
    
    When the Zen∴ctum ceremony ignited every forge simultaneously, the resulting heat surge struck the Ember Halls without warning. Kess was among three miners who collapsed at their stations. She never regained full use of her flippers. She was assigned to tend the colony's memorial fires — a duty described as honor, performed with hands that barely function.
    
    At some point Kess attempted a cartographic survey of the Glow-Fissure, a corruption site in the Nightshelf's lower tunnels then controlled by the Midnight Claws. She returned speaking in phonemes no colony-mate could parse, and reportedly left Nightshelf within a season. No source confirms she reached Aurora Stack. Yet subsequent accounts place her in the colony during the Mbra∴silentiu. The record does not reconcile these claims.
    
    ### The Crypt-seal☽ Teneecloris~ Trial
    
    During the Mbra∴silentiu, Kess was one of three miners selected to handle Crypt-seal☽ Teneecloris~, a shard recovered from the Ofundis∴flux crystallization beneath Sleek☽ Caemomot. Relic-handling custom required each tester to speak their name. The first two complied and died. Kess held the shard in silence for eleven seconds, beak shut, and upon releasing it spoke a single word: *Keelo* — the name of a miner lost in the convergence below.
    
    She did not speak again. Her daughter carried her fire-cores to market. Miners left rations in the lower tunnels without comment. The ice around her habitual sitting-places in the deep passages is reported to have aged beyond its stratigraphy — a claim I cannot verify from Foundation depth, but which I do not dismiss. She refuses to ascend to the upper caverns, even when inheritance disputes in the storage vaults require her tallying expertise.
    
    Kess kept counting until counting was taken from her. Then she kept still.
