  annotation "note_1771593144367_0", anchor: "Kess's numbers were not refuted. They were reclassified.", text: "The Rofundis∴rupt later collapsed ☽'scar Ramtatus~'s primary vein. If the anomaly Kess detected — heat consumed before harvest — was a precursor to that structural failure, then the reclassification suppressed not an inconvenient finding but an early warning. Two observers, separated by at least one generation, reported the same phenomenon in overlapping shafts. Both were overridden by production quotas set under Flipper Accord obligations. The second secret renegotiation of the Accord includes a draft annex on 'subterranean resource variance reporting.' It was never ratified. The collapse came after.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771593144367_1", anchor: "Kess held the shard in silence for eleven seconds", text: "Precise duration. Nightshelf relic-handling protocols log contact time in counted heartbeats — standard practice under ☽'ofund' Guild supervision. Eleven seconds at resting heartrate yields roughly fourteen to sixteen beats. The number is plausible as a formal measurement, not a reconstruction.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771593144367_2", anchor: "reportedly left Nightshelf within a season. No source confirms she reached Aurora Stack.", text: "A penguin returns from the Glow-Fissure speaking in phonemes no colony-mate can parse, departs the colony, cannot be traced to any destination, then reappears during a period when the veil between living world and ice-memory would have been operationally thin. The entry frames this as a gap in the record. It may be a gap in the subject. Corruption exposure at the Glow-Fissure produces documented alterations — cold-burn discoloration, whisper-echoes, perception of presences. The question is not where Kess went. The question is whether whatever returned was continuous with whatever left.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
